TinyJPEG is a header-only C++ port of Bodmer's "TJpg_Decoder" Arduino
library (https://github.com/Bodmer/TJpg_Decoder), which itself incorporates
ChaN's "TJpgDec" (Tiny JPEG Decompressor) engine. Three licenses apply,
covering the three layers of authorship - see docs/architecture.md for
which files fall under which:

===============================================================================
1. src/tjpgd.h (ChaN's TJpgDec engine, merged into one header - see that
   file's own header comment for the mechanical differences from the
   original two-file split; every algorithm and table is otherwise
   unchanged) - TJpgDec's own license:

/----------------------------------------------------------------------------/
/ TJpgDec - Tiny JPEG Decompressor R0.03
/-----------------------------------------------------------------------------/
/ The TJpgDec is a generic JPEG decompressor module for tiny embedded systems.
/ This is a free software that opened for education, research and commercial
/  developments under license policy of following terms.
/
/  Copyright (C) 2021, ChaN, all right reserved.
/
/ * The TJpgDec module is a free software and there is NO WARRANTY.
/ * No restriction on use. You can use, modify and redistribute it for
/   personal, non-profit or commercial products UNDER YOUR RESPONSIBILITY.
/ * Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice.
/
/----------------------------------------------------------------------------/

===============================================================================
2. Design and API inherited from Bodmer's "TJpg_Decoder" Arduino library
   (the block-callback decode model, the drawJpg/getJpgSize naming, the
   scale/swap-bytes options) - Bodmer's original license for that library:

